# JuggleJs coding conventions

## Stack rules

- Do not introduce frameworks, bundlers, or build steps unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer one focused change in `app.js` over new abstractions or extra files.
- CSS stays inline in HTML `<style>` blocks unless the user asks otherwise.

## Style

- Match existing `app.js` patterns: plain functions, minimal dependencies, English comments.
- Keep diffs small and scoped to the task.
- Reuse existing helpers: `pushBallState`, `displayVideoDetections`, `liveSnakeVisualisation`, `runOneDetectionFrame`, `setJuggleCount`.

## Runtime

- TFLite model requires a local server or GitHub Pages — not `file://`.
- Respect browser autoplay: video/audio/voice need a user gesture to start.
